no-std
import
	../bool
	../number

| Functions for using randoms are in 'keen/random/util'.
| This interface has a variety of functions to maximize performance;
| implementations need to maintain state to support the functions with `max-exclusive`
| while a plain {next32} or {next64} is often simpler internally.
|
| `generator-util.keen` can help implement this interface based on just {next32} or {next64}.
+random interface mut
	| Get a random number less than the maximum.
	next nat32(max-exclusive nat32)
	| Get a random number less than the maximum.
	next nat64(max-exclusive nat64)
	| Randomly {true} or {false}
	next-bit bool()
	| Random number from 0 to max-value::nat32 (inclusive)
	next32 nat32()
	| Random number from 0 to max-value::nat64 (inclusive)
	next64 nat64()
